# HTTPS front door for StreamVault on your home network (fixes plain HTTP on WiFi).
#
# 1. Install Caddy: https://caddyserver.com/download (a single caddy.exe on Windows)
# 2. Set SV_HOST to this computer's LAN IP or name, e.g. 192.168.1.20 or streamvault.local
# 3. From this folder run:   caddy run
# 4. Trust Caddy's local certificate on each device (README, "HTTPS on your network")
#
# Caddy serves the web app and the API on one HTTPS address. Start the server and the
# web app so they only listen on this computer (README shows how), so the plain-HTTP
# ports are not reachable from the WiFi.
{$SV_HOST:streamvault.local} {
	tls internal

	handle /api/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
	}
}
